{"content":[{"c":["FIERY SERPENT*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Bronze symbol of a snake made by Moses on God’s instruction to save the Israelites."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Deadly snakes were sent by God to punish the Israelites for their rebellious grumblings, many of whom died from the poisonous bites (",{"href":"?bref=Num.21.4-9","r":"Num.21.4-9","rawR":"Num.21.4-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.21.4-9","value":"Num.21.4-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 21:4-9"},"). Recognizing their sin, they cried out to God for deliverance, and he instructed Moses to make a fiery (bronze) serpent and set it on a pole. Healing was granted to those who gazed at the uplifted figure."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Jesus Christ referred to the bronze serpent incident as a symbol of the saving power of his crucifixion. A person who looks in faith to the uplifted Christ will receive deliverance from sin and have eternal life (",{"href":"?bref=John.3.14-15","r":"John.3.14-15","rawR":"John.3.14-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.3.14-15","value":"John.3.14-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 3:14-15"},"). The apostle Paul also drew upon the OT event as a warning to those who might arrogantly test God (",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.10.9","r":"1Cor.10.9","rawR":"1Cor.10.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.10.9","value":"1Cor.10.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 10:9"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=BronzeSerpentBronzeSnake_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"BronzeSerpentBronzeSnake_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"BronzeSerpentBronzeSnake_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Bronze Serpent, Bronze Snake"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"FierySerpent","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 21:4-9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.21.4-9","rawQueryValue":"Num.21.4-9","sourceRefExact":"Num.21.4-9"},{"anchorText":"Jn 3:14-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.3.14-15","rawQueryValue":"John.3.14-15","sourceRefExact":"John.3.14-15"},{"anchorText":"1 Cor 10:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Cor.10.9","rawQueryValue":"1Cor.10.9","sourceRefExact":"1Cor.10.9"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"00c9e97a6be41abfdadd01049f88ce1a58ef88e03289ff5db489ad63f77094fb","sourceItemName":"FierySerpent","sourceItemOrder":30,"sourceMember":"Articles/F.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"FierySerpent","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Fiery Serpent*","title":"Fiery Serpent*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}